cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EasySatSim in your research, please cite this software. The related paper is currently under review.
  The citation information will be updated after the paper is formally published.
title: EasySatSim
type: software
authors:
  - name: EasySatSim Contributors
abstract: >-
  EasySatSim is an extensible experimental framework for LEO satellite network research, designed to enable researchers to build customizable satellite network environments on personal computing devices.
  The framework organizes simulation logic around entities, behaviors, and the protocol stack, integrating large-scale constellation state evolution with packet-level communication processes in a unified experimental environment.
  This design enables researchers to construct and extend satellite network experiments according to specific research needs.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - satellite networks
  - network simulation
  - low Earth orbit
  - protocol stack
  - routing
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-15
repository-code: https://github.com/imust-lezhang/EasySatSim